<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Seminole War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1835">1835</a>–<a href="/years/1842">1842</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Florida War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Seminole War was fought from 1835 to 1842 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and the Seminole of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, who resisted removal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-territory">Indian Territory</a>. Led by chiefs such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osceola">Osceola</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/micanopy">Micanopy</a>, the Seminole waged a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war in the swamps that cost the United States heavily in money and lives. Most Seminoles were eventually removed west, but a few hundred stayed in Florida.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-seminole-war.jpg" alt="Second Seminole War" width="308" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pilaklikaha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
